- "The PFC has been $4.50 since April 1, 2001. Every serious attempt to raise it during the 2018, 2020, 2022, and 2024 FAA reauthorization debates was defeated by the airline lobby. Any funding thesis that requires a PFC increase is a thesis that requires an act of Congress that has failed for two decades."

- "NFPA 72 (2022) Section 18.4.11 requires that voice evacuation systems achieve a Speech Transmission Index of at least 0.45, or a Common Intelligibility Scale score of at least 0.7, throughout every area of coverage. That is the floor. A 'quiet' terminal is one designed so that this floor is comfortably clearable at rest, not one designed to sit below it."

- "The DCA perimeter rule dates to the early 1960s. Section 502 of the FAA Reauthorization Act of 2024 moved ten slots — the largest change in a decade. A proposal to move an operating rule at MWAA is a proposal to reopen a Senate Commerce Committee fight that the Authority itself will lobby to keep closed."

- "MWAA's Board is 17 seats across four appointing jurisdictions: Virginia (7), D.C. (4), Maryland (3), and the White House (3), with Senate advice-and-consent on the federal seats. A design-manual revision that changes the program scope or the airline rate base runs the airline MII gate and lands on that Board. Assume 12 months from draft to adopted resolution and expect to defend it in front of two state legislatures and one Senate committee."

- "The 2025 Use & Lease runs through December 31, 2039. Every quiet-by-design cost is retro-fitted onto a signed 15-year residual-cost framework, not a blank sheet — which is the strongest reason to write the standard *now*, before the Dulles transformation scope hardens into airline-approved CIP line items."

