## 5. What the Strategist should not assume is fixable on project timelines

- The PFC cap.
- The DCA perimeter and slot regime.
- ADA and NFPA compliance envelopes.
- CBP and TSA sovereignty over their own zones.
- The four-jurisdiction Board dynamic — appointments run on political calendars, not CIP calendars.

## 6. What is genuinely movable on the operator's decision calendar

- The MWAA Design Manual (Board resolution; internal drafting cycle).
- PFC application scope amendments within the $4.50 cap (14 CFR Part 158 process).
- Consultant scopes and construction specifications for Concourse E post-opening validation, and — critically — the pre-design specification package for the new Concourses C/D and central walking tunnel *before* the July 2026 program hardens.
- Airline-tenant PA governance policies as part of the next Use & Lease side-letter cycle or Design Review Committee protocol.
- Grant applications under the BIL Airport Terminal Program while its authorized funding runs through FY2026 (existing authority) and whatever reauthorization posture emerges for FY2027–2028.

